1	/**
2	 * Monitor Extension
3	 *
4	 * Mirrors Claude Code's "Monitor" tool. The LLM starts a long-running shell
5	 * command and each stdout/stderr line is streamed back as a notification —
6	 * no polling, no `bash | sleep | cat` loops, no token waste.
7	 *
8	 * Tools:
9	 *   - monitor_start(command, description, cwd?)  -> monitorId
10	 *   - monitor_status(monitorId, tailLines?)
11	 *   - monitor_read(monitorId, mode?, maxLines?)
12	 *   - monitor_stop(monitorId)
13	 *   - monitor_list()
14	 *
15	 * UI:
16	 *   - Footer status when ≥1 monitor is active (e.g. "● 2 monitors · alt+shift+m")
17	 *   - /monitors  command   – open the monitors dialog
18	 *   - alt+shift+m shortcut – open the monitors dialog
19	 *   - Down arrow on an empty editor – open the monitors dialog
20	 *   - Esc on an empty editor (with active monitors) – stop the most recent
21	 *   - In the dialog: ↑↓ select · enter view detail · x kill · esc close
22	 *
23	 * Reference: Claude Code prompt – "Use the Monitor tool to stream events from
24	 * a background process (each stdout line is a notification). For one-shot
25	 * 'wait until done,' use Bash with run_in_background instead."
26	 */
27	
