    "Rebuild and roll cluster image (C1) using claude-bridge-rollout.md §3: docker buildx build with REF=fdf9ac4, push to ghcr, update base/app.yaml image tag, commit+PR+merge, flux reconcile."
  ]
}
The prescribed end-state (versioned registry seam: Layer 1 fork packages + Layer 2 extensions published to GitHub Packages under @valkyriweb scope, Layer 3 per-runtime version pins, Changesets-automated release loop) is substantially implemented and functional. Both repos have working Changesets configs, auto-PR release workflows, CI gates, and actively published packages. The registry is live: @valkyriweb/pi-coding-agent has 3 published versions (0.78.0–0.78.2), @valkyriweb/my-pi-full has 5 (0.1.1–0.1.8, with a gap at 0.1.4–0.1.6), and a Version Packages PR (#86) is currently open in my-pi awaiting merge. The primary structural gaps are: (1) pi-mono-fork local main is 2 commits behind origin/main (PRs #45 and #46 merged upstream but not pulled locally), meaning the live binary built from the unmerged PR #47 branch includes changes from origin/main via a merge commit but the local main branch itself is stale; (2) pi-mono-fork has 20 commits since its last release tag (0.78.2) with no pending changeset, so those merged features will not trigger a release; (3) Layer 3 per-runtime lockfile pinning is documented but not implemented — no runtime directory has a pinned package.json + lockfile consuming a versioned @valkyriweb/my-pi-full; (4) branch protection is off on both repo mains; (5) pi-stack-inventory.md MacBook runtime entry still shows stale binary info from 2026-05-16.

